CAT = "s63Agents"; SEG = "AGT"
Q = [
("Which form does a firm file to register an individual agent with the states?",
 "Form U4", ["Form BD", "Form ADV Part 2", "Form U5"],
 "Form U4, the uniform application for securities industry registration, registers agents and IARs through the CRD system. Form BD registers the firm, and Form U5 ends an individual's registration."),
("A bank employee sells the bank's own stock to its customers and gets no extra pay for it. Under the USA she is:",
 "Not an agent", ["An agent of the issuer", "An agent of a broker-dealer", "An investment adviser rep"],
 "Bank securities are exempt securities, and an individual representing the issuer in transactions in them is excluded from the agent definition. Selling them for a broker-dealer would require registration."),
("An employee of a county sells the county's own bonds to investors. Under the USA she is:",
 "Excluded as an agent", ["An agent who must register", "A broker-dealer", "An investment adviser"],
 "An individual representing an issuer in transactions in certain exempt securities, including government and municipal securities, is excluded from the agent definition. Selling the same bonds for a broker-dealer would require registration."),
("A corporation's officer sells shares of its new, non-exempt public offering and is paid per sale. Under the USA she is:",
 "An agent of the issuer", ["Not an agent, as an officer", "A broker-dealer", "Excluded as an insider"],
 "Officers and directors are agents only if they otherwise meet the definition. Selling a non-exempt offering in a non-exempt transaction for pay does meet it, so she must register."),
("An agent of a broker-dealer sells only U.S. Treasury bonds to customers. Under the USA the agent:",
 "Must still register", ["Is excluded from registration", "Needs only a notice filing", "Registers only with the SEC"],
 "The exclusion for selling exempt securities covers individuals representing the issuer. An individual representing a broker-dealer must register as an agent whatever the securities sold."),
("A receptionist at a broker-dealer only answers phones and schedules meetings. Under the USA she is:",
 "Not required to register", ["An agent of the firm", "A registered principal", "An investment adviser rep"],
 "Clerical and administrative staff who do not effect or attempt to effect securities transactions are not agents. Soliciting orders or recommending securities would change that."),
("An agent may transact securities business in a state only while she is:",
 "Registered, with a registered firm", ["Registered in her home state only", "Supervised by a principal of any firm", "Under a signed customer contract"],
 "Agent registration is tied to a broker-dealer or issuer. The agent must be registered in the state where she does business, and the firm she represents must also be registered or exempt."),
("An agent leaves Firm A to join Firm B. Under the USA, who must promptly notify the Administrator?",
 "The agent and both firms", ["Only the agent herself", "Only Firm A, the old firm", "Only Firm B, the new firm"],
 "When an agent begins or ends a connection with a broker-dealer or issuer, the agent as well as the firm must promptly notify the Administrator, so both firms and the agent report the move."),
("A registered agent is charged with a felony. Her firm must amend her Form U4 no later than:",
 "30 days after learning of it", ["10 days after a conviction only", "60 days after learning of it", "At her annual renewal"],
 "Form U4 amendments are due within 30 days after the firm learns of the facts. A felony charge is reportable when it is filed, not only on conviction."),
("When a firm files Form U5 for a departing agent, it must also:",
 "Give the agent a copy", ["Send a copy to each customer", "Get the agent's signature", "Post it on its website"],
 "FINRA's by-laws require the firm to provide the individual with a copy of the Form U5 at the same time it is filed, so the agent can respond to anything reported."),
("An agent of Firm A opens an account at Firm B with Firm A's consent. Under FINRA Rule 3210, if Firm A asks in writing, Firm B must:",
 "Send duplicate statements", ["Close the agent's new account", "Bar the agent from any trading", "Report each trade to FINRA"],
 "Rule 3210 requires the executing firm, on written request from the employing firm, to transmit duplicate confirmations and statements or the transactional data contained in them."),
("Which account at another firm does NOT need the employer's consent under FINRA Rule 3210?",
 "A 529 plan account", ["A margin account", "A cash brokerage account", "An options account"],
 "Rule 3210 does not apply to accounts limited to redeemable investment company shares, unit investment trusts, 529 plans and similar products. Brokerage accounts of any kind need prior written consent."),
("An agent wants to pay her unregistered accountant a fee for each account he refers. Under FINRA Rule 2040 this is:",
 "Prohibited", ["Allowed if disclosed", "Allowed as a flat fee", "Allowed for retail accounts"],
 "Rule 2040 bars paying transaction-based or other compensation to anyone who would have to be registered to receive it. A per-account referral fee to an unregistered person is that kind of payment."),
("Under FINRA Rule 2040, a retiring agent may keep receiving commissions on accounts she served if:",
 "A contract existed before she left", ["Her clients sign waivers", "She keeps her registration", "The Administrator approves each payment"],
 "Continuing commissions to a retired registered person are allowed under a bona fide contract entered into while registered, provided the person does not solicit new business or open new accounts."),
("Absent an order from the Administrator, an agent's registration becomes effective:",
 "At noon on the 30th day after filing", ["Five business days after filing", "When FINRA approves it", "Ten days after filing"],
 "Under the USA, a broker-dealer, agent or adviser registration becomes effective at noon of the thirtieth day after a complete application is filed, unless the Administrator acts sooner or a proceeding is pending."),
("An agent registered only in State A phones a prospect in State B to recommend a stock. She:",
 "Must be registered in State B", ["Needs only State A registration", "Needs only her firm's approval", "Is outside State B's reach"],
 "An offer is made in a state when it is directed to and received there. Calling a resident of State B to recommend a security is doing business there and requires registration in State B."),
("Under the USA, an officer of a broker-dealer who solicits customer orders is:",
 "An agent who must register", ["Excluded because she is an officer", "A broker-dealer herself", "An issuer"],
 "A partner, officer or director of a broker-dealer is an agent if she performs the functions of an agent, such as soliciting orders. Officers with purely managerial duties are not."),
("FINRA Rule 3210 consent is needed for an account at another firm held by an agent's:",
 "Spouse who lives with her", ["Adult sibling in another city", "Former college roommate", "Cousin with no shared funds"],
 "Rule 3210 covers accounts in which the agent has a beneficial interest, which includes those of a spouse or other immediate family member living in the same household or supported by the agent."),
("Which event must be reported on an agent's Form U4?",
 "A customer complaint alleging fraud", ["A minor speeding ticket on vacation", "A change in marital status", "A new personal bank account"],
 "Form U4 discloses certain written customer complaints alleging sales practice violations, criminal charges, regulatory actions and financial events. Minor traffic offenses are not reported."),
("An agent registered in her home state wants to solicit residents of three other states. She needs:",
 "Registration in each state", ["Only her home state registration", "A federal agent license", "Only her FINRA registration"],
 "Each state registers agents who do business with its residents. FINRA registration does not replace state registration, and no federal agent license exists."),
("A broker-dealer hires a trainee whose agent registration is still pending. Until it takes effect, the trainee may:",
 "Do clerical work only", ["Call prospects to pitch funds", "Take orders from friends", "Recommend specific stocks"],
 "Soliciting, taking orders and recommending securities all require effective registration. Before then, the trainee may do only administrative and clerical tasks."),
("An individual represents an issuer in a private placement that qualifies for the USA's limited offering exemption, with no commission paid. She is:",
 "Outside the agent definition", ["An agent who must register", "A broker-dealer for the offering", "An underwriter only"],
 "The USA excludes from the agent definition an individual representing an issuer in exempt transactions. If a commission were paid for soliciting buyers in the limited offering, the exclusion would be lost."),
("With an application for agent registration, the USA requires the applicant to file:",
 "A consent to service of process", ["A personal surety bond from a bank", "A personal credit report", "Proof of a college degree"],
 "Every applicant for registration must file an irrevocable consent appointing the Administrator to receive service of process in suits arising from its securities business. Form U4 contains this consent."),
("Under FINRA Rule 2040, a firm may pay transaction-based compensation to:",
 "Its registered agent", ["An unregistered finder", "A customer's accountant", "A retired agent with no contract"],
 "Payments tied to securities transactions may go only to persons appropriately registered (or to retired persons under a qualifying prior contract). Unregistered finders and accountants may not be paid per transaction."),
("A registered agent buys shares for herself through another firm without telling her employer. This violates:",
 "FINRA Rule 3210", ["FINRA Rule 2040", "Regulation S-P", "FINRA Rule 2210"],
 "Rule 3210 requires the employing firm's prior written consent before an associated person opens or keeps an account at another firm, and the agent must tell the executing firm of her association."),
("Which person must register as an agent under the USA?",
 "A part-time salesperson for a firm", ["A firm's mailroom clerk", "The registered broker-dealer itself", "A bank teller who cashes checks"],
 "Anyone who represents a broker-dealer in effecting securities transactions is an agent, whether full time or part time. Clerical staff and bank tellers are not, and the firm registers as a broker-dealer."),
]
